  "context": "## Car Evolution Mobility OS – Evidence Cases 03-07\nCase 03 · Tallinn old town edge · access window 07:30–09:30 · policy as a number Source: POLITICA_CHOICES +3 to N, POLITICA_TRANSBORDOS_CHOICES CT DIN FO LO NT NP, valor_politicas , valor_puntualidad , valor_ocupacion , valor_ahorro_unidades\n\nThe policy scale is not a switch. It runs from +3 to −5 , and it is asymmetric on purpose: the penalty for an option we want avoided is heavier than the reward for one we prefer. That is how a city reasons about restriction, and it was in the constants a decade ago.\n\nEvery point carries its own transfer policy, including one that is not a pickup point at all. Toompea is refused, and the refusal is a policy value rather than an omission.\n\nTwo weightings are scored side by side and the authority takes B. Punctuality falls from 0.91 to 0.78. The cost is recorded next to the choice , because the decision has to survive being asked about in public, and a decision whose price was never written down cannot.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 7.41%; Use cases and applications 7.41%; Decisions and responsibility 22.22%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 18.52%; Memory, community and territory 7.41%; Mobility and infrastructure 37.03%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/car-evolution-mobility-os-evidence-cases-03-07-e1959/\nSource document: https://jubap.eu/mobility/evidence/case-03-07/\n\n",
